  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In February 2026 Senate responses, Rudd agreed that China is aggressively seeking advanced AI chips and that such chips are foundational to AI superiority, and he warned that procurement delays would impair military innovation. In April 2026 testimony as NSA director, Rudd described AI research and development as a constant and AI as central to the transformation of warfare, and said the agency continues to invest in AI and automation. In January 2026, Rudd said the widespread proliferation of AI and other disruptive technologies amplifies complex threats by placing advanced capabilities in more actors’ hands. A reported personal statement attributed to Rudd said AI will make “us” faster and more effective.",
   "sids": [
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s5",
    "s1",
